ader_compile_binary_from_spirv(Ve\n \t\toffset += sizeof(uint32_t);\n \t\tencode_uint32(sizeof(ShaderBinary::Data), binptr + offset);\n \t\toffset += sizeof(uint32_t);\n+\t\toffset += sizeof(uint32_t); // Pad to align ShaderBinary::Data to 8 bytes.","path":"drivers/vulkan/rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp","commit_id":"e674379764e0864a001a0859bf3ee36eef4a8340","original_commit_id":"79911235792135b600c93cf2d2b65c34f6205f37","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> To make sure we don't get regressions from `ShaderBinary::Data` changing size in the future, should we have some `static_assert` for the assumption we're making here / above / below?\r\n\r\nThe actual size of `ShaderBinary::Data` is dynamically determined. And it changing size wouldn't change alignment of it. The problem was that we had it 12 bytes into the structure, but the `ShaderBinary::Data`  structure has `uint64_t vertex_input_mask = 0;`. This means that the whole structure needs to be aligned to 8 bytes, not 4. That is what the extra padding is for.\r\n","created_at":"2024-12-12T21:54:35Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T21:55:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100325#discussion_r1882940377","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100325","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1882940377"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100325#discussion_r1882940377"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100325"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1882940377/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":3473,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1882488261,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":13,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1882949849","pull_request_review_id":2500867429,"id":1882949849,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5wO4jZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -3470,6 +3470,7 @@ Vector<uint8_t> RenderingDeviceDriverVulkan::shader_compile_binary_from_spirv(Ve\n \t\toffset += sizeof(uint32_t);\n \t\tencode_uint32(sizeof(ShaderBinary::Data), binptr + offset);\n \t\toffset += sizeof(uint32_t);\n+\t\toffset += sizeof(uint32_t); // Pad to align ShaderBinary::Data to 8 bytes.","path":"drivers/vulkan/rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp","commit_id":"e674379764e0864a001a0859bf3ee36eef4a8340","original_commit_id":"79911235792135b600c93cf2d2b65c34f6205f37","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Hi everyone! Regarding the changing of `sizeof(ShaderBinary::Data)` see [my reply](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100325#issuecomment-2540095483).\r\n\r\nA static_assert would indeed make things safer, but ultimately the responsibility of guarding that is in the function being modified by this PR, because it's a **_versioned_** binary data. The PR forgot to bump `ShaderBinary::VERSION`.\r\n\r\nOf course a static_assert would add an extra layer of reminders \"hey! remember to bump `ShaderBinary::VERSION`!\".","created_at":"2024-12-12T22:03:27Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T22:03:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100325#discussion_r1882949849","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100325","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1882949849"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100325#discussion_r1882949849"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100325"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1882949849/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":3473,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1882488261,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":13,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/